{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "mos-xy16-preserve-x-p-save",
  "title": "XY16 X preservation saves $p as defined after a call clobbered its flags",
  "status": "fixed",
  "reproducer_origin": "original",
  "report": "docs/investigations/2026-09-27-near-index-overflow-proofs.md",
  "summary": "MOSInsertREPSEP::preserveX decides whether its PH $p reads a defined status register from backward liveness. A scavenger status-register save elsewhere in the loop makes N/Z look live across blocks, so after a JSR that clobbered them preserveX emits PH $p without undef and the machine verifier rejects it. Found as the one candidate-only failure of the near-index proof replay on the extracted upstream series (boids.c, XY16). Given the IR carrying the recovered nuw flags, the prerequisite alone, the candidate and the downstream compiler all fail identically; the same source compiles on the downstream compiler because its earlier passes produce different IR. Only machine verification rejects it; without -verify-machineinstrs the object is emitted.",
  "attribution": [
    "Found and recorded during near-index proof upstream extraction: Claude Code 2.1.283, model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), xhigh reasoning effort; session f79adc39-72b4-4dc5-abc1-849c14c5ce96.",
    "Recovered-IR reproduction first reported by the independent reviewer of the near-index proof packet (docs/pr-preparations/2026-09-29/near-index-proofs/independent-review.md) and replayed by the recorder.",
    "Repair, validation and closure: Claude Code 2.1.295 (t4-opus-high agent a469d5bd6fc11cf09), model Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort; session 72f6d6de-6687-477a-bb4c-b186f9d1ba7f."
  ],
  "unknowns": [
    "The shared install build/llvm-mos-install is still the old-pin compiler 6f303945, which retains the defect; the fixed new-pin toolchain is installed at the separate prefix build/llvm-mos-f24948c7d1a4-install. Swapping the shared install to the new pin is a separate decision.",
    "The record baseline (c8fb18cb) is the near-proof upstream candidate; the green candidate is the downstream compiler at the October 10 pin with the repair. The same-source pair at that pin is the unfixed f24948c7d1a4 build (2acf2f54, exit 134 on the identical input and configuration) and the fixed build (f68dae29, exit 0).",
    "The October 9 green toolchains were host g++ rebuilds of one translation unit; they were removed after the container-built toolchain reproduced every result."
  ],
