  "resolution": {
    "change": "patches/llvm-mos/0002-321-accum16.patch: MOSInsertREPSEP::preserveX needed-value test (live after the save point and defined before it) for the PH $p and PHA16 $a16 undef flags and the PLX shortcut, with live_undefined_nz and live_undefined_p in insert-rep-sep-cloned-kills.mir; folded into split-series #321-4 by round seven (b393bb94db76).",
    "causal_explanation": "preserveX decided whether its A/P courier saves read defined values from backward liveness alone. A later push of all of P (the scavenger PHP, valid because carry is defined there) keeps N, Z and V live back through a JSR that clobbered them, so after the call preserveX emitted PH $p without undef and took the shuffle instead of PLX. The machine verifier walks forward, finds no defined part of P, and rejects the push. Requiring forward availability, the verifier's own criterion, marks the push undef and lets PLX restore X; it never fires where N/Z hold a defined value.",
    "trigger_check": "The record input reaches the failing PH $p in main %bb.25: the baseline and the unfixed October 10 build both report it there and exit 134, and the fixed build exits 0. Two MIR functions exercise the operation directly (live-but-undefined N/Z with and without a stack byte in the region); they fail on #321-4, the old installed llc, the near-proof candidate and the unfixed new-pin llc, and pass with the repair. The recovered IR and the truchet -O3 XY16 sighting fail before and pass after on the new pin. MOS lit 202 pass, 4 unsupported; corpus-a16 83/83; xy16xreload 8/8 MAME+bsnes-jg. Census at the pin, clang-built before/after llc on frozen IR: 5,088 configurations, objects byte-identical except boids.c XY16 -Os (-19 B) and truchet.c XY16 -O3 (-59 B), the only two that failed the verifier before. Both ROMs, rebuilt from each llc's object, return their host oracle (boids 0xA8AB, truchet 0xB3E6) on bsnes-jg and MAME before and after.",
